RE: Retail Liquor License
Dear Mayor and City Council,
By introduction my nameis Hans Kuhlmann, Managerand sole memberof Halifax Development, LLCand Doughdog,
LLC.Halifax Development, LLC and Doughdog, LLC are retail development companies based in Denver, Colorado.For
thepast twoyears wehave been looking for are tail development site in Cheyenne along the Del Range corridor.This
past March we entered into a Real Property Purchase Agreement with Georg anne Walker EtAl, Karen Armour Trust and
Jo Anne Hendryx, the owners of thetwelve acrevacant tractof landlocated on the northwest corner of Del Range and
Powderhouse,(the Hendry x Property").We are alsoin negotiations with the Airport Authority for a1.68acrevacant
property onthenorth sideof Del Range thatis surrounded bythe Hendry x Property.The Hendry x Property is currently
in Laramie County and is zoned a combination of Low Density Residential(LR)and Medium Density Residential(MR)and
the Airport Property is located in the City of Cheyenne and is zoned Medium Density Residential(MR-1).Both
Properties are currently located in the flood way and floodplain.It is our intention to annex the Hendry x Property into
the Cityof Cheyenneand rez one both the Hendry x Property and Airport Propertytoa commercial zoning that permits
the development of retail, restaurant, hoteland office uses.Attached tomy License and/or Permit Application for a
Retail Liquor License is a preliminary siteplan of our proposed development.We have interest in this site from a
numberof national restaurants, some of which serve alcohol and will need the retail liquor license to operate.Thesite
2017.Should youhaveany questions please do not hesitateto contactme.
With bestregards,
Hans F Kuhlmann
Manager and Sole Member of Halifax Development, LLC and Dough dog, LLC
